## Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the bosphorus-vibe Next.js project.

### Changes Made

#### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (version 1.1.0)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` to reflect the installation

#### 2. Code Integration
Modified `src/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<body>` element in the root layout

### Implementation Details

According to the official Vercel Speed Insights documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), for Next.js v13.5+ projects:
1. The package should be imported from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
2. The `<SpeedInsights />` component should be placed in the root layout file
3. The component automatically tracks page performance metrics once deployed to Vercel

The implementation follows the framework-specific instructions for Next.js (this project uses Next.js 14.2.29, which is compatible with the recommended approach).

### Verification

✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ All routes compiled and generated static pages (29/29)
✅ No TypeScript or compilation errors introduced
✅ The SpeedInsights component is now active and will collect performance data when deployed to Vercel

### Next Steps

To start collecting Speed Insights data:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel (via `vercel deploy` or through Git integration)
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Speed Insights)
3. After deployment and user visits, performance metrics will be available in the Vercel dashboard

### Files Modified
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated lock file with new package and dependencies
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights import and component
